cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AMP Classifier — trained antimicrobial peptide discriminator with cluster-aware splits"
abstract: >-
  A binary antimicrobial peptide / non-AMP classifier trained on the
  DRAMP 3.0 corpus with mmseqs2 cluster-aware splits at 40% sequence
  identity to prevent the redundancy-driven AUC inflation typical of
  naive splits in the AMP literature. ESM2-650M frozen embeddings plus a
  small MLP head reach AUC 0.919 [0.906–0.931] on the cluster-aware test
  set, beating an XGBoost baseline over 428 engineered features (AUC
  0.864 [0.845–0.880]) with non-overlapping 95% bootstrap CIs.
